course: dictionary
lesson: 15003
title: Resemble: looking alike
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To resemble someone or something means to look like them, or to be similar to them. Resemble is a verb, so it changes its ending: resembles, resembled, resembling.
explain: «My little sister resembles our mum: they both have curly hair and a big smile.» The sentence tells you what the likeness is, so you can work out the meaning from the clues.
explain: Animals often resemble the things around them. «The stick insect resembles a twig.» A thing that resembles another is similar to it, though it may not be exactly the same.
fact: Resemble means to look like someone or something, or to be similar to it.
fact: «Lucy resembles her dad» means Lucy looks like her dad.
fact: «The stick insect resembles a twig» means it looks like a twig, which helps it hide. This is called camouflage.
fact: In maths, shapes that resemble each other may be similar: they have the same shape, but not always the same size.
fact: «Closely resemble» means look very alike, and «bear a resemblance to» means have a likeness to someone or something.
exercise: «The twins closely resemble each other.» What does resemble mean here? | Sing together | *Look very alike | Argue with each other | Live in different towns
exercise: «The stick insect resembles a twig.» What does this sentence tell you? | It is bigger than a tree | It is hungry | It is a twig | *It looks like a twig
exercise: Which form of resemble shows something that happened in the past? | *resembled | resemble | resembling | resembles
test: «Tom bears a resemblance to his uncle, with the same dark eyes.» What does bears a resemblance to mean? | *Looks like, or is similar to | Is taller than | Lives near | Is cross with
test: Which sentence uses resemble correctly? | The dog resembled hungry | The dog resembled to run | The dog resembled the sofa very loudly | *The dog resembled a wolf, with thick grey fur
exam: Which word in «Zara closely resembles her mum, but she resembles her dad when she laughs.» means to look like or be similar to? | *Resembles | Closely | Laughs | Mum
